{{- /*
The crash claim's defect: the rebuild finds an empty medium.

Correct while it runs and amnesiac across the seam — every write lands
and every one is gone the moment the process is built again. That is the
whole of what crash recovery claims, stated in one line.

The subject is the reference, which is a working implementation: the
defect has to be right about everything else, or the schedule reds on
the first read rather than on the first read AFTER a crash, and the
message names the wrong thing.
*/ -}}
{{- define "suite.defect.fresh-medium" -}}
{{ renderExpr (external $.Prove "One") }}({{ printf "%q" .DefectName }},
	func({{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}) {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Subject) }} {
		return {{ renderExpr (external .Pkg .Ref) }}()
	}).RecoveringFresh(){{ template "suite.frag.defect-reason" . }}
{{- end -}}
